## 8.3 Items Requiring Separate Scope or Add-On Pricing

Some activities may be related to the original project but require additional scope, pricing, and approval because they add complexity, risk, or delivery effort.

These may include:

* Additional workload domains
* Additional physical sites
* NSX Federation
* vSAN stretched cluster
* VCF Automation beyond foundational setup
* VKS production enablement beyond initial scope
* Advanced vDefend Firewall or microsegmentation design
* NSX ALB / AVI advanced configuration
* VMware Live Recovery / SRM implementation
* HCX migration enablement
* Air-gapped or disconnected lifecycle management
* Regulated or highly restricted environments
* Complex certificate or identity requirements
* Custom automation
* Extended documentation
* Additional knowledge transfer sessions
* Extended hypercare
* After-hours or weekend change windows
* Onsite delivery
* Rescue or remediation of pre-existing issues

These items may be quoted as fixed-price add-ons, hourly services, or Expert Bank consumption, depending on the situation.

---

## 8.4 Partner and Customer Responsibilities

Successful delivery depends on timely participation and readiness from the partner and customer.

Unless otherwise agreed, the partner and/or customer are responsible for:

* Providing accurate technical information
* Providing access to required systems
* Ensuring licenses are available and valid
* Ensuring hardware is available, supported, and ready
* Providing network, DNS, NTP, firewall, and certificate prerequisites
* Assigning technical contacts and decision-makers
* Providing change windows
* Approving designs and implementation plans
* Coordinating internal teams
* Managing customer communications
* Managing commercial and contractual relationship with the end customer
* Reviewing and approving deliverables in a timely manner

Delays in these responsibilities may affect project timelines, delivery dates, and pricing.

---

## 8.5 Documentation Boundaries

Klaud provides documentation related to the agreed technical scope. Documentation is intended to support architecture understanding, implementation traceability, operational handover, and partner/customer enablement.

Standard documentation may include:

* Design documents
* Implementation notes
* As-built documentation
* Validation results
* Technical findings
* Risk and recommendation summaries
* Knowledge transfer material

The following documentation is excluded unless specifically included:

* Formal regulatory compliance documentation
* Audit certification reports
* Full operational manuals
* End-user manuals
* Training curriculum development
* Custom-branded customer documentation
* Extensive diagramming outside agreed scope
* Documentation for systems not implemented or reviewed by Klaud

---

## 8.6 Hypercare Boundaries

Some fixed-price bundles may include a limited post-deployment hypercare period. Hypercare is intended to support stabilization after project delivery, not to provide long-term managed support.

Hypercare may include:

* Follow-up technical questions
* Validation support
* Minor configuration review
* Issue triage related to delivered scope
* Clarification of documentation
* Handover support

Hypercare does not include:

* New feature implementation
* Additional integrations
* New workload domains
* Major design changes
* 24x7 production support
* Customer operational administration
* Issues caused by changes made outside the agreed scope
* Support for unrelated systems or third-party tools

Any work beyond the agreed hypercare scope may be handled through hourly services, Expert Bank hours, or a separate fixed-price engagement.

---

## 8.7 Scope Validation Requirement

All services are subject to scope validation before final commitment. The pricing in this catalog provides a commercial framework, but final scope and pricing may vary depending on:

* Customer environment size
* Number of sites
* Number of workload domains
* Version compatibility
* Hardware readiness
* Network complexity
* Security requirements
* Migration complexity
* Operational constraints
* Change window limitations
* Documentation requirements
* Timeline expectations
* Customer readiness

Klaud reserves the right to adjust pricing, delivery assumptions, or engagement model if the technical assessment identifies complexity, risk, or requirements beyond the standard scope.
